{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem\n`shim.py::_to_common_finding` (the translation feeding `review_code()`'s public `review_result`\noutput -- the `rebar review-code` CLI and the `review_code` MCP tool) carries `severity`\nforward from each kernel-shaped finding but drops the numeric `priority` (`validity x impact`)\ncomputed by `pass3_decide`. A caller of `review_code()` -- the live, real consumer of this\ntranslation -- sees only the impact-only severity label, never the priority the kernel itself\ndecided BLOCK/ADVISORY with.\n\nCORRECTION to the epic's original problem statement: `aggregate.py::aggregate_findings` (the\n\"cross-finding aggregation/dedup picks the highest-severity representative\" consumer named in\nthe epic) is confirmed DEAD CODE -- it has no caller anywhere in `src/rebar/` (grep confirms\nzero call sites outside its own definition and the `__init__.py` re-export), orphaned since\nADR 0075 retired the single-pass code-review route that used to feed it. The CURRENT four-pass\npipeline's real cross-finding dedup (`_cluster_findings` in `code_review/workflow_ops.py:149`,\nplus `dedup_key`/`suppress_and_dedup` in `review_kernel/decide.py:252`) picks a representative\nby first-in-stable-order, NOT by severity or priority -- so there is no live severity-based\nmisranking bug in the current dedup step, and `aggregate.py` needs no change in this epic.\n(Separately, the Gerrit review-bot comment already reads `priority` directly off the kernel\nverdict via `adapter.py::_translate_findings`, bypassing `shim.py` entirely -- so this ticket's\nfix is specifically for the `review_result`/`review_code()` consumer, not the Gerrit path,\nwhich the sibling ticket patriotic-abdicative-arrowana covers separately.)\n\n## Approach\nThread `priority` AND `decision` through `code_review/shim.py`'s `_to_common_finding` so the\n`review_result` shape `review_code()` returns carries the numeric priority and the\nblock/advisory decision already computed by `pass3_decide` (or set on DET-tier findings by the\nsibling priority-backfill ticket), alongside the existing `severity` field (which is not\nremoved by this ticket -- see the epic's expand-contract sequencing).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] `shim.py::_to_common_finding` includes `priority` AND `decision` in its output dict for\n  every finding, alongside the unchanged existing `severity` key.\n- [x] `pytest tests/unit/test_code_review_ws4.py -k test_shim_translates_kernel_findings_to_common_findings`\n  passes, strengthened with an assertion that the translated common finding carries the same\n  `priority` and `decision` values as the source kernel finding.\n- [x] `src/rebar/llm/aggregate.py` and `src/rebar/llm/spec_scan.py` have zero diff from this\n  ticket (`git diff --stat src/rebar/llm/aggregate.py src/rebar/llm/spec_scan.py` is empty) --\n  both are out of scope (the former is dead code, the latter is a sibling ticket).\n\n## Testing\nTier: in-process unit test against the real `shim.py::_to_common_finding` translation function,\nfed a production-shaped kernel finding dict (contract test: real producer shape -> real\nconsumer). Oracle: the exact `priority`/`decision` values on the translated common finding,\nasserted alongside the existing `severity` assertion. `test_shim_translates_kernel_findings_to_common_findings`\n(test_code_review_ws4.py:180) is the RED oracle to strengthen."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788130826343302110,"uuid":"fafe50d4-054c-4997-b962-5cd17e862536"}